==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|ru|ǵʰreh₃d}}
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*gradъ}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*greh₃d-}} or {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰreh₃d-}}. Cognate with {{cog|lt|gruodas}} ({{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*grōda-}}), {{cog|la|grandō}}, {{cog|xcl|կարկուտ}}, {{cog|sa|ह्रादुनि|t=hail}} and possibly with {{cog|en|grind}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|n=sg}}

# {{lb|ru|meteorology}} [[hail]]
#: {{uxi|ru|Град [[идти|идёт]]|It’s hailing.}}
# [[volley]], [[shower]]
#: {{uxi|ru|град [[пуля|пуль]]|hail of bullets}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|n=sg}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|ru|cu|градъ}}, which is a reflex of {{der|ru|sla-pro|*gordъ||settlement, enclosed place}}. {{doublet|lang=ru|го́род}} which was normally inherited by [[w:pleophony|pleophony]]. Old Church Slavonic word shows [[w:liquid metathesis|liquid metathesis]] characteristic of South Slavic area.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+}}

# {{senseid|ru|town}} {{lb|ru|poetic|antiquated}} [[town]], [[city]], used as a common city name suffix ([[Волгоград]], [[Калининград]], [[Ленинград]])
#: {{uxi|ru|[[стольный]] град|capital (city) (''modern Russian'': {{m|ru|столица}})}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|го́род}}
* {{l|ru|-град}}

===Etymology 3===
Borrowed from {{bor|ru|la|gradus}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|град.|m-in|-}}

# {{ru-abbrev of|гра́дус||[[degree]]}}

[[Category:ru:Weather]]
